-- ============================================================================
-- EC2 ASSOCIATE DEEP SEED: Fiscal Regime Design, beginner tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: ONE REGIME'S LEDGER, with every instrument held flat.
-- What the four instruments are, what the sandbox GENERATES rather than
-- takes, the fixed 25 year horizon, the closed-form decline, three streams,
-- the price deck's step hold, fixed and variable opex, capex in year one,
-- gross revenue, a flat royalty, cost recovery at the full limit, profit oil
-- at a flat split, tax on the profit share, contractor net cash flow,
-- government take, cumulative cash flow, payback and the totals. It ends
-- able to read one concession end to end and knowing that one regime alone
-- answers no comparative question.
--
-- THE SANDBOX GENERATES ITS OWN FORECAST, and that is the shape of the tier.
-- There is no production input beyond an initial rate and a decline, no
-- input that changes the 25 year horizon, and no capex schedule: the whole
-- of the capital is charged in year 1. A reader who arrives expecting to
-- supply a profile is not being refused a feature, they are using the wrong
-- tool, and the tier says which tool is the right one.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The decline is applied AFTER the year is
-- booked, so year 1 carries the initial rate times 365 days with no decline
-- taken, and the price deck is a STEP function that holds a price until the
-- next point and never interpolates. Both mistakes push a reader's year 1
-- and their step year in the same direction, and neither shows up as an
-- error: the ledger simply comes out wrong by a few percent everywhere.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. Contractor take and government take do
-- NOT sum to revenue minus cost in a year where cost recovery binds, because
-- the unrecovered balance is carried forward rather than paid to anybody.
-- At a 100 percent cost recovery limit the two do agree, which is why a
-- concession is the right ledger to learn on and a production sharing
-- contract is not.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the ledger
-- columns themselves.
-- ============================================================================

